w the turn. The pot remains small. Betting here has little utility; worse hands (high cards) will likely fold, and better hands (Kx, Jx, 7x) will call or raise. Checking allows me to see the river for free, realizing my showdown value without bloating the pot with a marginal hand.\n\nReason: My hand has some showdown value but is vulnerable. Checking back is the most prudent play to control the pot size and see if the hand improves on the river.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
